# A small board to bring up for the first time: 9 V in through a reverse-polarity diode (1N4007), a 7805 regulator to 5 V,
# a power LED with 330 ohm and a 1k load. The first power-on guide (学ぶ → 最初の電源投入のガイド, or `poweron` here) gives the
# current the 9 V supply should deliver, the range of a working board and the current limit to set on the bench supply.
# Build: cargo run -p cli -- docs/examples/power_on.ccad
new
add V 9 as=V1
add 1N4007 as=D1
add LM7805 as=U1
add C 330n as=C1
add C 100n as=C2
add R 330 as=R1
add LED as=D2
add R 1k as=R2
net VIN V1.+ D1.A
net VREG D1.K U1.IN C1.1
net 5V U1.OUT C2.1 R1.1 R2.1
net LEDA R1.2 D2.A
net GND V1.- U1.GND C1.2 C2.2 D2.K R2.2
erc
dc
poweron
poweron measured=60m
save docs/examples/power_on.schjson
